<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azzone Visconti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1302–1339</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Azzone Visconti was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> from 1329 to 1339. He bought the title of imperial vicar, rebuilt Milan's walls and public buildings, and extended Visconti rule over the neighbouring communes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, including Bergamo, Como, Cremona, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a>, Novara, Vercelli, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brescia</a> and Piacenza. His conquests turned the lordship of Milan into a regional state that later became a duchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/azzone-visconti.jpg" alt="Azzone Visconti" width="320" height="346" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Azzone_Visconti.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
